117
00:09:11,350 --> 00:09:18,590
Scott: You've got like a little bit more safety hoping that, you know, it's like the best possible binning of the CPU.

118
00:09:18,990 --> 00:09:21,230
Scott: It's not actually faster or better.

119
00:09:21,350 --> 00:09:26,262
Rym: Well, the interesting thing is right now for the Intels, the price difference between the i7 and the i9 is like 130 to 150 bucks.

120
00:09:29,950 --> 00:09:35,410
Scott: Yeah, that's a lot of money for basically when you look, even the benchmarks, which, you know, are only telling you so much.

121
00:09:35,952 --> 00:09:39,630
Scott: The difference between them benchmark wise is like almost nothing.

122
00:09:40,070 --> 00:09:41,570
Scott: It's like they're nearly identical.

123
00:09:41,710 --> 00:09:44,470
Rym: Well, the stat I zeroed in on was not so much.

124
00:09:44,670 --> 00:09:47,005
