499
00:32:50,568 --> 00:32:51,150
Scott: That's the rule.

500
00:32:51,790 --> 00:32:56,810
Scott: So obviously if you're a rules lawyer, you know, like we are, there's all sorts of questions, right?

501
00:32:57,070 --> 00:32:59,890
Rym: What if I'm in a gasoline powered wheelchair?

502
00:33:00,852 --> 00:33:01,353
Scott: Right, right.

503
00:33:01,433 --> 00:33:04,780
Scott: Most of the question is what qualifies as a vehicle?

504
00:33:04,800 --> 00:33:09,950
Scott: And the second question is, are there other circumstances, right?

505
00:33:10,650 --> 00:33:16,950
Scott: It's like, is this an absolute rule or is there a circumstance that would allow something even if it was a vehicle?

506
00:33:17,110 --> 00:33:28,870
Scott: So it basically takes this rule, which is obviously too vague a rule to be covering everything that needs to be covered, and then asks you a bunch of yes or no questions of like, is this allowed?

507
00:33:29,251 --> 00:33:29,873
Scott: Is this allowed?

508
00:33:30,235 --> 00:33:30,897
Scott: Is this allowed?

509
00:33:31,318 --> 00:33:34,730
Scott: And then compare, it shows you the data on what everyone else has answered, right?

510
00:33:35,491 --> 00:33:36,974
Scott: So you can take different approaches.

511
00:33:37,014 --> 00:33:44,610
